# CODEOWNERS — the exclusive-ownership model of docs/PROJECT_MANAGEMENT.md, enforced
#
# §8.2 makes concurrent agents safe by giving each track a disjoint set of paths, and
# §8.3 lists the small, merge-hostile files that no track agent may touch. Until now
# that model lived only in prose, and Phase 1 fans out to four tracks at once. This file
# is the same table, in the one place GitHub reads before a merge.
#
# What it actually buys: a review request on every PR that crosses a boundary. It does
# not stop a commit, so §8.2 stays the rule and this is the tripwire.
#
# Rules: last matching pattern wins, so the defaults come first and the boundaries below
# override them. Keep the order.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TODO — owner handles
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @Ssisakhti is the only GitHub identity this repository can verify: it is the owner
# segment of `origin` (github.com/Ssisakhti/X2KNWLDG) and matches the committer address
# `Ssisakhti@users.noreply.github.com`. Every track therefore resolves to that one
# account today — correct for a single-maintainer project, and *not* the four-way split
# §8.2 describes.
#
# When a track gets its own GitHub account or team, replace the owner on that track's
# lines only; do not change the paths without changing §8.2 first. The four names to
# fill in, if teams are ever created:
#
#   Track A — Indexer            → TODO: @<handle-or-team>
#   Track B — API                → TODO: @<handle-or-team>
#   Track C — Frontend           → TODO: @<handle-or-team>
#   Track D — Fixtures & tests   → TODO: @<handle-or-team>
#   Integrator (§8.3)            → TODO: @<handle-or-team>
#
# Do not invent a handle here. An owner GitHub cannot resolve is silently dropped, and
# the boundary it was protecting then has no owner at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @Ssisakhti

